{"ratings":[{"id":"C1","consequence":"secret","trigger":"unusual","reason":"A cut through an ANSI sequence can leave part of a registered credential in stored output and model feedback under a contrived output pattern."},{"id":"C2","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"unusual","reason":"A short credential matching a phase name can cause a resumed run to skip its remaining stages and be recorded as successful."},{"id":"C3","consequence":"secret","trigger":"unusual","reason":"A symlink target containing a registered credential can expose it in the stored coverage file list after canonicalization."},{"id":"C4","consequence":"secret","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A multiline credential supplied through the environment can be reconstructed in a stored failure excerpt when a gate prints it."},{"id":"C5","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A downloaded patch can silently differ from the stored patch, causing an operator to act on inaccurate evidence."},{"id":"C6","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Removing literal escape sequences from the inline patch can cause a reviewer to miss a relevant change."},{"id":"C7","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"The API-wide transformation can silently alter a patch artifact, reproducing the inaccurate evidence described in C5."},{"id":"C2b","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Restoring a command snapshot containing literal escape sequences can produce a false blocking audit finding and stop the resumed run."}]}